Normalize a raw browser-copy text dump from a selectable PDF into semantic-ingestion-friendly Markdown.

Designed for the Schopenhauer "On Vision and Colors" browser-copy paste, but intentionally
kept generic enough for other book-like PDF text dumps.

Core contract:
- The raw input is never modified.
- Normalization is conservative and reportable.
- The output is Markdown structured for downstream semantic chunking.
- The script prefers preserving questionable text over silently "improving" it.

Example:
    python normalize_browser_pdf_text.py \
        "Pasted text(7).txt" \
        --out-dir normalized_output \
        --title "On Vision and Colors"

Outputs:
    normalized_output/
      normalized.md
      normalization_report.json
      manual_review_flags.md
      duplicate_candidates.json
